1205 0 obj
<<
/Title (announcement section. External CSS is used for the main website design. External CSS is the best choice for a multi-page website because one stylesheet can be reused across all pages. 2. Selectors: Element selector, class selector, ID selector, group selector, descendant selector, child selector, attribute selector, pseudo-class and pseudo-element are included. Hover and focus states are also provided. 3. Box Model: Every event card contains content, padding, border and margin. Example calculation: content width 250px + left/right padding 24px + left/right border 2px = 302px total horizontal width under content-box. Border-box: If width is set to 250px with box-sizing:border-box, the total width remains 250px because padding and border are included within the declared width. 4. Layout: CSS Grid is used for the event catalogue. Four columns are used on large screens, two on medium screens and one on small screens. The HTML order remains logical. 5. Positioning: Sticky navigation, relative event cards, absolute status badges, fixed help button and z-index are demonstrated. These elements are positioned so they do not cover important form fields or content. 6. Other CSS properties: The design uses background colours, gradients, border-radius, box-shadow, text-shadow, opacity, overflow, cursor, transition, transform, list-style and max-width. 7. Responsive design: Media queries change the navigation, event cards and registration form for smaller screens. At about 375px the cards appear in one column and horizontal scrolling is avoided.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1199 0 R
/Prev 1204 0 R
>>
endobj
